<title>USA: Philip Morris to make $6.5 bln case payment.</title>
<headline>Philip Morris to make $6.5 bln case payment.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Philip Morris Cos Inc is expected to pick up about $6.5 billion of the initial $10 billion payment called for under the recent settlement struck with cigarette makers, the New York Times said.</p>
<p>In Wednesday's edition, the newspaper said the payment is part of a formula agreed upon by the five tobacco companies participating in the proposal, with the first payment to be determined based on the stock market value of each company.</p>
</text>
